  "question": {
    "text": "The value of the integral $\\int_{1}^{2} e^{x}\\left(\\log _{e} x+\\frac{x+1}{x}\\right) d x$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "DP6D6",
      "text": "$e^{2}\\left(1+\\log _{e} 2\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Fb2Ln",
      "text": "$e^{2}-e$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5PcDN",
      "text": "$e^{2}\\left(1+\\log _{e} 2\\right)-e$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pGBIA",
      "text": "$e^{2}-e\\left(1+\\log _{e} 2\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $I=\\int_{1}^{2} e^{x}\\left(\\log _{e} x+\\frac{x+1}{x}\\right) d x$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad I=\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(e^{x} \\cdot \\log _{e} x+e^{x}+\\frac{e^{x}}{x}\\right) d x$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad I=\\int_{1}^{2} e^{x} \\log _{e} x d x+\\int_{1}^{2} e^{x} d x+\\int_{1}^{2} \\frac{e^{x}}{x} d x$\r\n$-\\int_{1}^{2} e^{x} \\log _{e} x d x$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad I=\\left(e^{2}-e^{1}\\right)+\\left(e^{2} \\log _{e} 2-0\\right)$\r\n$=e^{2}\\left(1+\\log _{e} 2\\right)-e$",
    "image": null
  },
